WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.949 --> 00:00:02.368
- [Narrator] Let's play a game.

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.608
Think of a famous painting.

00:00:04.608 --> 00:00:05.441
Guess what?

00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:07.478
You just thought of me.

00:00:07.478 --> 00:00:09.787
Today, I'm the world's
most renowned work of art,

00:00:09.787 --> 00:00:11.696
but it wasn't always this way.

00:00:11.696 --> 00:00:14.045
My story is full of surprises,

00:00:14.045 --> 00:00:16.849
and it all began in a studio in Florence.

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:20.349
(upbeat orchestral music)

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.569
Well, here's the master
himself, Leonardo da Vinci.

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:30.036
He worked on me on and off for a few years

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:31.492
towards the end of his career.

00:00:31.492 --> 00:00:32.823
- You're a minor work, my dear,

00:00:32.823 --> 00:00:34.624
some interesting shading, nothing more.

00:00:34.624 --> 00:00:37.176
- [Narrator] We'll just see about that.

00:00:37.176 --> 00:00:40.855
Over the next 300 years, I
hung quietly in French palaces

00:00:40.855 --> 00:00:42.666
and royal bathrooms.

00:00:42.666 --> 00:00:44.163
The things I've seen.

00:00:44.163 --> 00:00:46.445
- [Napoleon] I want you.

00:00:46.445 --> 00:00:48.596
- [Narrator] Until finally I
was noticed by a man who had

00:00:48.596 --> 00:00:51.369
already made quite a name for himself.

00:00:51.369 --> 00:00:53.484
When Napoleon chose me to
hang on his bedroom wall,

00:00:53.484 --> 00:00:55.122
people took notice.

00:00:55.122 --> 00:00:57.382
- I look forward to sleeping
with you, my cherie.

00:00:57.382 --> 00:00:59.630
- [Narrator] After he had his
whole exile from France thing,

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.760
they tossed me on a wall at The Louvre.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.700
But at this point, I was still

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.689
just another Renaissance portrait.

00:01:07.689 --> 00:01:08.859
Until one night.

00:01:08.859 --> 00:01:12.692
(daunting, suspenseful music)

00:01:13.988 --> 00:01:15.150
- Bella.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.337
- [Narrator] I was stolen!

00:01:16.337 --> 00:01:17.465
It was pandemonium.

00:01:17.465 --> 00:01:19.215
Paris was in an uproar.

00:01:19.215 --> 00:01:22.065
The police hauled people
in left and right.

00:01:22.065 --> 00:01:23.385
The hysteria hit a fever pitch

00:01:23.385 --> 00:01:25.326
when the police suspected and interrogated

00:01:25.326 --> 00:01:29.285
one of the most famous artists
in the world, Pablo Picasso.

00:01:29.285 --> 00:01:30.788
(officer speaking French)
(man gasping)

00:01:30.788 --> 00:01:32.230
But Picasso was innocent.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:35.134
The thief turned out to
be an Italian carpenter.

00:01:35.134 --> 00:01:37.025
He was caught in Florence.

00:01:37.025 --> 00:01:37.858
- Mama mia.

00:01:37.858 --> 00:01:40.590
- [Narrator] And I returned to The Louvre.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.459
From that day forward,
I became the darling

00:01:42.459 --> 00:01:44.139
of the art world.

00:01:44.139 --> 00:01:46.359
Everyone wanted to see
Napoleon's da Vinci painting

00:01:46.359 --> 00:01:48.890
Picasso was suspected of stealing.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.321
Soon, tourists crowded
in and most people forgot

00:01:51.321 --> 00:01:53.750
why I was famous in the first place.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.711
That might raise some
eyebrows, but not mine

00:01:55.711 --> 00:01:57.243
since I don't have any.

00:01:57.243 --> 00:01:59.898
Oh, you didn't notice I
don't have any eyebrows?

00:01:59.898 --> 00:02:03.091
I told you, I'm full of surprises.

00:02:03.091 --> 00:02:06.174
(soft chiming music)

